<article class="env-lemma" id="06MJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06MJ">Lemma <span data-tag="06MJ">74.9.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces. If $f$ is locally of finite presentation, flat, and surjective and $X$ is locally Noetherian, then $Y$ is locally Noetherian. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a scheme $V$ and a surjective étale morphism $V \to Y$. Choose a scheme $U$ and a surjective étale morphism $U \to X \times _ Y V$. As $f$ is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation the morphism of schemes $U \to V$ is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation. In this way we reduce the problem to the case of schemes (as being locally Noetherian for $X$ and $Y$ is defined in terms of being locally Noetherian of $U$ and $V$, see Properties of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/03E5" data-tag="03E5">66.7</a>). In the case of schemes the result follows from Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/034C" data-tag="034C">35.16.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>